  "worked_solution": "The rate of change of the particle's $y$-coordinate when $t=1$ is given by ${y}^{\u2032}(1).$\n\nIn step 5, we found that\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}(t)=\\frac{6-12{t}^{2}}{2{t}^{3}+3t}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(1) & =\\frac{6-12(1)^{2}}{2(1)^{3}+3(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-12}{2+3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
